      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T22:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The host command protocol already provides a versioning mechanism.  I don\u0027t think this is needed to future proof the command.  I also can\u0027t think of an instance where we would have 64-bit support, but only needed a single offset for all memory regions.  It seems more likely we would need to each `struct ec_response_memory_dump_get_entry_info` to include a 64-bit address.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5579,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 5580,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
