      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T22:07:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could use `SYS_INIT()` to have the zephyr memory dump module self initialize instead of requiring a public routine.\n\nAlso, should this be done after `vboot_main()` - in which case you would need to use `DECLARE_HOOK(HOOK_INIT,...)` instead of `SYS_INIT`.  The kernel runs `SYS_INIT` calls before starting the application main function.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "89c246dcb380439fc088e14e6df9f4c6600d0191",
